cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Awesome Looped Transformers: papers, code and blogs on recurrent-depth Transformers"
message: >-
  If you find this repository useful for your research,
  please cite it using the metadata from this file (or via
  the "Cite this repository" button on the GitHub page).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Hejian"
    family-names: "Sang"
    alias: "HJSang"
abstract: >-
  Awesome Looped Transformers is a curated, continuously updated list of
  papers, open-source code, released models, and technical blogs on looped
  (recurrent-depth, weight-tied, universal, recursive) Transformers:
  architectures that reuse a shared block of layers several times inside a
  single forward pass to trade compute for effective depth. Entries are
  annotated by loop topology, depth control, input injection, training origin,
  and scale, and organised into surveys and foundations, theory, mechanistic
  analysis, pretrained looped language models, stability and scaling laws,
  adaptive depth, retrofitting pretrained LLMs, efficient training and
  serving, latent-reasoning objectives, recursive reasoners (HRM/TRM/DEQ),
  applications, production models and reports, frameworks, and blogs.
keywords:
  - "looped transformers"
  - "recurrent depth"
  - "depth recurrence"
  - "universal transformers"
  - "weight tying"
  - "latent reasoning"
  - "test-time compute"
  - "adaptive computation"
  - "deep equilibrium models"
  - "large language models"
  - "awesome list"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HJSang/awesome-looped-transformers"
url: "https://github.com/HJSang/awesome-looped-transformers"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-04"
